WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:01.090
John: Good morning Hank, it's Tuesday.

00:00:01.090 --> 00:00:05.160
Given that the Quadragocon was a tie, I suppose
that we're going to have to do a Quadragocon

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:06.580
again in 2016.

00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:07.779
So I already started training.

00:00:07.779 --> 00:00:10.440
But unfortunately during my first training
session I pulled my hamstring.

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:13.761
I wish that were a joke but you can probably
tell from the way that I'm walking that it's

00:00:13.761 --> 00:00:14.761
not.

00:00:14.761 --> 00:00:16.110
Anyway I'm gonna become someone else today.

00:00:16.110 --> 00:00:17.780
Okay I'm here on the Crash Course Government
set.

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:21.349
So Hank as you know Sarah and I have a show
with PBS Digital called the Art Assignment,

00:00:21.349 --> 00:00:25.050
where we go around the country and we talk
to contemporary artists and they give you

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:26.050
an art assignment.

00:00:26.050 --> 00:00:29.279
One of those assignments, Tameka Norris's
"Become Someone Else", has really stuck with

00:00:29.279 --> 00:00:33.450
me so I wanna try it today and I invited my
friend and our office manager Zulaiha-

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:34.450
Zulaiha: Hey!

00:00:34.450 --> 00:00:37.560
John: - long time nerdfighter to join and
also become someone else.

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:38.560
Zulaiha: Yep.

00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:41.270
John: So the idea is to like change one thing
about your physical appearance and then take

00:00:41.270 --> 00:00:46.400
a before selfie and an after selfie of like
who you've become in that process.

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:47.400
Zulaiha: Yep.

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:50.020
Except I'm gonna cheat a little and change
my entire outfit.

00:00:50.020 --> 00:00:51.290
John: She's gonna cheat.

00:00:51.290 --> 00:00:52.290
Zulaiha: Yep.

00:00:52.290 --> 00:00:54.260
John: But I'm gonna play by the rules because
that's who I am as a person.

00:00:54.260 --> 00:00:56.640
Okay so first things first let's take our
before selfies.

00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:58.190
You're current you right now.

00:00:58.190 --> 00:00:59.190
Zulaiha: Yep.

00:00:59.190 --> 00:01:00.430
John: And then I'm gonna be current me.

00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:04.999
[Singing] Selfie Interlude Music because people
on YouTube really hate silence.

00:01:04.999 --> 00:01:05.999
Zulaiha: Ding!

00:01:05.999 --> 00:01:09.119
So I'm going to change from my everyday regular
clothing that I wear when I'm in "western

00:01:09.119 --> 00:01:13.119
clothing" that is, to traditional clothing
that people like my mom wear everyday and

00:01:13.119 --> 00:01:15.710
just don't give two [censored] about what
people think, um because I have a lot of respect

00:01:15.710 --> 00:01:21.512
for people like that and who just don't care
and aren't self conscious about that kind

00:01:21.512 --> 00:01:22.512
of thing.

00:01:22.512 --> 00:01:23.512
John: Do you feel self conscious when you
wear hijab in public?

00:01:23.512 --> 00:01:24.512
Zulaiha: No, surprisingly.

00:01:24.512 --> 00:01:26.969
John: 'Cause you just- it's just- part of
how you've always dressed

00:01:26.969 --> 00:01:28.010
Zulaiha: Yeah, I'm just used to it by now.

00:01:28.010 --> 00:01:29.740
John: So I am much more self conscious than
you.

00:01:29.740 --> 00:01:33.219
I get recognized a lot when I go out and it
makes me anxious.

00:01:33.219 --> 00:01:37.020
It's not bad, like I'm grateful to people
for coming up to me and everything, but it's

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:40.219
mostly what's weirdest is when people just
like take pictures from a distance.

00:01:40.219 --> 00:01:41.610
I can feel them looking at me.

00:01:41.610 --> 00:01:47.130
And I'm very nostalgic for some reason about
like 2007 to 2009 when everyone I would meet

00:01:47.130 --> 00:01:48.689
on the street were like nerdfighters.

00:01:48.689 --> 00:01:51.719
And it's terrible to be nostalgic for that
time because of course in the years since

00:01:51.719 --> 00:01:53.520
many things that I like have happened.

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:57.790
Like I have had children whom I am quite fond
of and like my book became very successful

00:01:57.790 --> 00:02:02.959
and became a movie and stuff but anyway I'd
still kind of like to become 2008 me and you

00:02:02.959 --> 00:02:04.340
know how I do that, Zulaiha.

00:02:04.340 --> 00:02:05.340
Zulaiha: By putting on hat?

00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:06.340
John: That's right.

00:02:06.340 --> 00:02:07.340
I put on a hat.

00:02:07.340 --> 00:02:08.340
Zulaiha Where are we going out to?

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:09.340
John: I thought we might go to-

00:02:09.340 --> 00:02:10.340
Zulaiha: Coffee?

00:02:10.340 --> 00:02:11.340
John: Coffee or Chipotle.

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:16.510
So per Tameka's instructions we are now going
somewhere, uh, dressed as our new selves.

00:02:16.510 --> 00:02:17.510
How do you feel?

00:02:17.510 --> 00:02:18.510
Zulaiha: Kind of the same.

00:02:18.510 --> 00:02:20.420
This is what happens when I never go to Starbucks.

00:02:20.420 --> 00:02:25.239
John: Uh, we forgot money, so Zulaiha's trying
to download the Starbucks app.

00:02:25.239 --> 00:02:27.840
So our trip to Starbucks was completely unsuccessful.

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:33.510
However we did go out in public and talk to
strangers as someone other than ourselves,

00:02:33.510 --> 00:02:34.510
right?

00:02:34.510 --> 00:02:35.510
Zulaiha: Yeah.

00:02:35.510 --> 00:02:36.510
Yeah.

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:37.510
We did do that.

00:02:37.510 --> 00:02:38.579
John: What was your experience?

00:02:38.579 --> 00:02:40.620
Zulaiha: Um, I didn't feel that much different,
to be honest.

00:02:40.620 --> 00:02:44.480
I think that's 'cause I associate wearing
these clothes with my family and I act different

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:47.430
around my family but I don't really act different
around you or at work.

00:02:47.430 --> 00:02:49.600
Or maybe I'm just more comfortable wearing
this kind of clothing than I thought I was

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:51.890
and I should just do it everyday.

00:02:51.890 --> 00:02:52.890
John: Yeah.

00:02:52.890 --> 00:02:54.180
[Singing] Selfie Interlude Music

00:02:54.180 --> 00:02:55.500
Zulaiha: How did your hat make you feel?

00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:59.100
John: Wearing the hat does make me feel like
someone else and someone I'm more comfortable

00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:02.780
being in public, so it's strangely effective.

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:04.909
[Singing] Selfie Interlude Music

00:03:04.909 --> 00:03:07.530
Hank, what I love about the Art Assignment
is that it makes me do and think about things

00:03:07.530 --> 00:03:10.160
I wouldn't usually do or think about.

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:13.860
In this case it made me think about what's
changed and what hasn't in the last few years.

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:18.280
Hank I think some kind of loss is inherent
to change but doing Tameka's assignment reminded

00:03:18.280 --> 00:03:21.200
me that I am always becoming someone else.

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:22.760
So thank you to Tameka Norris.

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:23.760
Check out the Art Assignment.

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:27.010
There are lots of great assignments and lots
of great videos about contemporary art.

00:03:27.010 --> 00:03:29.329
Hank I wonder if you had to become someone
else who you'd become?

00:03:29.329 --> 00:03:30.400
I'll see you on Friday.

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:31.400
Oh wait!

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:32.400
P.S.

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:34.329
The wonderful people at Penguin UK are doing
an awesome project to raise money for the

00:03:34.329 --> 00:03:35.620
Teenage Cancer Trust.

00:03:35.620 --> 00:03:38.720
It's got a Fault in Our Stars theme, so if
you live in the UK or Ireland please check

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:42.080
out nightofinfinities.co.uk Thanks bye!

